  "id": "COMPOUND:25877 - PROTEIN:710",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between (3beta,5alpha,7alpha)-3,7-Dihydroxyandrostan-17-one and ATP-binding cassette sub-family A member 1, as this compound is implicated in multiple pathways that target this protein. Specifically, the compound is linked to the cholesteryl ester transfer protein, which is a target of Cis-Bis(Methylthio)Silvatin, and also to (2R)-pentan-2-ol, which in turn targets ATP-binding cassette sub-family A member 1. These findings indicate that the compound may influence the function of ATP-binding cassette sub-family A member 1 through indirect pathways involving other proteins. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, but the exact mechanism remains unclear. The evidence highlights the compound's role in signaling or regulatory networks that ultimately affect ATP-binding cassette sub-family A member 1, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction.",
